The above code has basic functionality for adding and removing events. It uses mutex to ensure thread safety, which prevents data corruption when multiple threads access or modify the same data simultaneously. A logging mechanism (not implemented) would be a good addition to track system health and performance over time. Also, error handling is not included in this basic implementation but could be incorporated using `try-catch` blocks around potentially failing code sections.",deepseek-coder:33b,vanilla_random_search_run_5.csv,0,,False,1,1,0.0,"[{""block_id"": 1, ""language"": ""cpp"", ""error"": ""In file included from /usr/include/c++/9/bits/stl_algobase.h:71,
